# G052 — Bank Account

*v2. See `bank-account.md` for prose: double-entry ledger, zero-sum invariant,
atomic transfers, ledger-balanced as a global conservation check.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Monthly Sweep with Balanced Reconciliation

[monthly-sweep @month-start
    IN ORDER TO
        run a month-end reconciliation that three reviewers sign off on
        only if the global ledger conservation invariant holds

    @all-tx <- [bank[transactions-since {at: @month-start}]]

    concurrent [
        <- @kathryn{verify conservation of transactions: @all-tx}
        <- @sarah{flag overdrafts in: @all-tx}
        <- @ellie{sum fees from: @all-tx}
    ]
    join

    [bank[ledger-balanced]]
        where
            every account balance is non-negative
            and the sum of debits equals the sum of credits
            and kathryn's verification returned "confirmed"
        || -> #reconciliation-halted @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[bank
    open-account           {holder-id, kind}
    close-account          {id}                            ;; || non-zero-balance
    freeze                 {id}
    deposit                {account-id, amount-cents}
    withdraw               {account-id, amount-cents}      ;; || insufficient-funds
    transfer               {from-id, to-id, amount-cents}  ;; || either-frozen
    balance                {account-id}
    statement              {account-id, from?, to?}
    total-assets           {customer-id}
    transactions-since     {at}
    ledger-balanced                                          ;; global invariant check
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: double-entry invariant as verification step

The v1 insight: every transfer creates a pair of entries summing to
zero, and the global ledger must balance. In Innate, that's a
verification gate:

[bank[transfer {from-id: @a, to-id: @b, amount-cents: @n}]
    <- [bank[conservation-check]]
    where entries sum to zero and both accounts are active
]

`<-` verifies the transfer against reality before advancing. A
non-balanced transfer emits resistance, caught by the outer choreography.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @bank <- [bank[new]]
    (@bank, @alice) <- [bank[open-account
                               {holder-id: "alice", kind: "checking"}]]
    (@bank, @bob)   <- [bank[open-account
                               {holder-id: "bob", kind: "savings"}]]

    [bank[deposit {account-id: @alice, amount-cents: 10000}]]
    [bank[transfer {from-id: @alice, to-id: @bob, amount-cents: 3000}]]

    -> [bank[balance {account-id: @alice}]]   ;; -> 7000
    -> [bank[balance {account-id: @bob}]]     ;; -> 3000
    -> [bank[ledger-balanced]]                 ;; -> true
]
